\uc0\u61623  Propranolol\
Beta\
blocker that inhibits beta1 (heart) and beta2 (bronchial) receptors. It is used for\
many indications (essential tremor) in addition to BP control. BP decreases secondary\
to a decrease in HR.\
Bronchoconstriction\
may occur due to the effect on the B2 receptors.\
Wheezing\
in a client taking this drug may indicate bronchoconstriction or\
bronchospasm. \cf6 Nurse should assess for any history of asthma or resp problems with\
this client and notify the HCP.\
\cf0 Headache\
is common occurrence with HTN. Analgesic can be given as needed.\
It\
may take several days of treatment for the BP to reduce to a more normal finding.\
Reduction in HR is expected with betablockers.\
Nurse should monitor it for further reduction.\
